PATCH 508: three more cockpit-HUD methods -- 8024, 804b, 8072.

FUN_0000_8024 (asm 0x8024-0x8044) and FUN_0000_804b (asm 0x804b-0x806b) are the same glyph plate twice:
    8024: 8b 3e 34 6d     mov    di,[0x6d34]              ; the PLAYER's NEAR OFFSET
    8028: 0f b6 45 3f     movzbw ax,[di+0x3f]
    802c: 05 c8 04        add    ax,0x4c8                 ; (804b: 0x4d8)
    802f: 8d 5f 04        lea    bx,[bx+4]
    8032: 83 07 01        addw   [bx],1
    8035: 83 47 02 03     addw   [bx+2],3                 ; (804b: 0x2f)
    8039: ff 1e b4 06     lcall  [0x6b4]
    803d: 83 2f 01        subw   [bx],1
    8040: 83 6f 02 03     subw   [bx+2],3                 ; (804b: 0x2f)
BX is the display-list element's near offset (the 209e walk publishes it to DGROUP:0x3e08, patch 142).
Ghidra host-deref'd the element, emitted all four `addw/subw` as 4-byte int read-modify-writes (which
also clobber [bx+8..9]), and dropped both the player lookup and the far call's (ax,bx) argument pair.

FUN_0000_8072 (asm 0x8072-0x80b4), the turret-bearing readout:
    8072: mov ax,2 ; lcall 0f69:5bbe                  ; 524e(2) -- its AH feeds BOTH 530b calls
    807a: mov ax,0x54 ; mov bx,0x9a ; lcall 0f69:5c41 ; 52d1(0x54,0x9a)
    8085: mov al,0x44 ; lcall 0f69:5c7b               ; 530b
    808c: mov si,0x96b5 ; lcall 0f69:5e9b             ; thunk_5531 over DGROUP:0x96b5
    8094: mov al,0x39 ; lcall 0f69:5c7b               ; 530b with the SAME AH -- only AL is reloaded
    809b: mov di,[0x6d34] ; mov ax,[di+0x89]          ; the PLAYER's turret bearing WORD
    80a3: call 0x31c ; mov si,0x1f8c ; call 0x2c5 ; mov si,0x1f8e ; lcall 0f69:5e9b
Ghidra DISCARDED 524e's return value and used two uninitialised `extraout_AH` pseudo-vars for the two
530b calls, passed thunk_5531 the raw near offset 0x96b5 where it takes a HOST pointer (patch 139), and
dereferenced DAT_2000_2d34 as a host pointer.

8024 was the top SIGSEGV of the post-507 sweep (8024 <- 209e <- 206f <- 459a).
